// The REPL buffer (owner 2026-10-12): a scratch buffer, [REPL], holding every
// entry the session kept and every file %load kept — a refused entry stays
// out — whichever buffer colon mode is on. `madc -i FILE` is line mode, so
// colon mode starts on FILE; :ls lists both, :b NAME switches, an edit is one
// undo group, %run of [REPL] is refused (no file) and :q never counts it.
int base = 10;
